.TH MKFIFO 2P "August 1, 1992"
.ds ]W POSIX 1003.1
.SH NAME
mkfifo \- (POSIX only) make a FIFO special file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.ft B
#include <sys/types.h>
#include <sys/stat.h>
.PP
.ft B
int mkfifo(const char *\fIpath\fP, mode_t \fImode\fP);
.ft R
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The information in this specification applies
only to POSIX applications.
.PP
The
.IR mkfifo 
function
creates a new FIFO special file
whose pathname is pointed to by \fIpath\fP.
The mode of the new file
(including special file bits)
is initialized from \fImode\fP, modified by
the process's mode mask (see
.IR umask (2)).
.PP
The owner ID of the new FIFO is set to the effective user ID of the
calling process.  The group ID of the FIFO is set to the group ID of the
directory in which the FIFO is created.
.PP
Upon successful completion, the
.IR mkfifo 
function marks for update the \fIst_atime\fP, \fIst_ctime\fP and \fIst_mtime\fP
fields of the file, and the \fIst_ctime\fP and \fIst_mtime\fP fields of the
directory in which the FIFO is created.
.SH "RETURN VALUE"
Upon successful completion a value of zero is returned.
Otherwise, a value of -1 is returned, no FIFO is created and \fIerrno\fP
is set to indicate the error.
.SH "ERRORS"
If any of the following conditions occurs, the
.IR mkfifo 
function returns -1 and sets \fIerrno\fP to the corresponding value:
.TP 15
[EACCES]
Search permission is denied for a component of the path prefix.
.TP 15
[EACCES]
Write permission is denied on the parent directory of the FIFO to be created.
.TP 15
[EFAULT]
The \fIpath\fP argument points outside the process's allocated address space.
.TP 15
[EDQUOT]
The directory in which the entry for the new FIFO
is being placed cannot be extended because the
user's quota of disk blocks on the file system
containing the directory has been exhausted.
.TP 15
[EDQUOT]
The user's quota of inodes on the file system on
which the FIFO is being created has been exhausted.
.TP 15
[EEXIST]
The named file exists.
.TP 15
[EINVAL]
The pathname contains a character with the high-order bit set.
.TP 15
[EIO]
An I/O error occurred while making the directory entry or allocating the inode.
.TP 15
[ELOOP]
Too many symbolic links were encountered in translating the pathname.
.TP 15
[ENAMETOOLONG]
A component of \fIpath\fP exceeds {NAME_MAX} (see <limits.h>) characters,
or the entire pathname exceeds {PATH_MAX} (see <limits.h>) characters.
.TP 15
[ENOENT]
A component of the path prefix does not exist.
.TP 15
[ENOENT]
The \fIpath\fP points to an empty string.
.TP 15
[ENOSPC]
The directory in which the entry for the new FIFO is being placed
cannot be extended because there is no space left on the file
system containing the directory.
.TP 15
[ENOSPC]
There are no free inodes on the file system on which the
FIFO is being created.
.TP 15
[ENOTDIR]
A component of the path prefix is not a directory.
.TP 15
[EPERM]
The pathname contains a character with the high-order bit set.
.TP 15
[EROFS]
The named file resides on a read-only file system.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
chmod(2),
pipe(2),
stat(2P),
umask(2)
